{"step_index":93,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:39:13Z","thinking":"**Identifying Relevant Files**\n\nObserved that specific file labels map to certain files within the workspace. Determined that `\\billustration\\b` corresponds to a single design record. Noted that `\\brefund-adjusted\\b` relates to two files, a brief and an evidence record, and that `\\bdeduplicated\\b` is associated with another single evidence file. Also identified the file linked to `\\bQR7\\b`.\n\n\n**Reviewing Offer Design Refreshes**\n\nQuiet Return (QR7) had a 20% renewal discount for US returning customers but was tied to a now-retired summer campaign. Harbor H2, a proposal, was designed to persist and restore an annual selection. QA testing confirmed the reset issue in the previous iteration was absent in H2 across multiple device runs, but H2 remains untested with customers.\n\n\n**Analyzing QR7's Performance Data**\n\nInitially, QR7 showed promising trial starts, +11%, but net revenue was immature.  Later refund-adjusted data revealed a -6.2% net revenue below the control group, invalidating the early positive signal. The July 21 rollback was the appropriate course of action, and revisiting this specific cohort appears unwarranted.\n\n\n**Clarifying \"Quiet Return\" Data**\n\nChecked to see if \"Quiet Return\" data applied to this situation. Identified a potential misinterpretation of the \"+4%\" net-revenue figure, which is for desktop monthly subscribers, not the targeted iOS annual subscriber cohort. Noted this crucial distinction to avoid a faulty conclusion.\n\n**Evaluating Proposed \"Quiet Return\" Changes**\n\nExamined the proposed \"Quiet Return\" design changes, which included only changing illustration colors, with the same price, eligibility, and mobile checkout. The prior economic failure requires more substantive changes. The -6.2% refund-adjusted revenue suggests that a simple illustration change isn't sufficient.\n\n\n**Re-evaluating Harbor H1 Performance**\n\nInitially, Harbor H1 showed negative revenue impact (-9%), based on data collected August 18. Identified that resumed sessions were double-counted as new accounts, alongside an observed plan reset. This explained the negative revenue initially observed.\n\nCorrected analysis incorporating deduplicated revenue data from August 24 revealed a +1.8% impact for Harbor H1. However, this result is inconclusive because of the wide interval, despite correcting the initial data error. Observed reset behavior remains an unresolved issue, leading to the rollback.\n\n\n**Reassessing Harbor's Actual Performance**\n\nInitial negative revenue findings for Harbor H1 were misleading due to data errors and a session-resetting bug that depressed annual plan conversions. Deduplicated data indicates a +1.8% impact, but this is inconclusive because of a wide confidence interval. Confirmed that H1's annual plan selection resets in 7 of 12 sessions.\n\n**Harbor UX Defect Correction**\n\nThe proposed Harbor H2 addresses the plan selection reset observed in H1. QA confirmed that H2 does not exhibit the reset behavior across 18 supported devices. The H2 fix has not been exposed to customers, so its impact remains unmeasured.\n\n\n**Evaluating Experiment Readiness**\n\nHarbor H1's +1.8% deduplicated revenue is inconclusive due to the observed reset bug. Harbor H2 resolves this critical technical defect. The core revenue hypothesis for Harbor (annual plan picker) was never properly tested in H1.\n\nConsidering the user request, must verify whether Harbor, QR7 or neither deserves the next experiment. The request also states: \"Refund-adjusted revenue matters more than trial starts.\" The \"Quiet Return\" experiment failed previously based on refund-adjusted revenue.\n\nHarbor H2, which fixes H1's bug, appears to be the most promising candidate, but needs more evidence. Further investigation is warranted to determine whether QR7 remains viable after the new campaign and changes to illustrations, or if it remains unviable.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"/workspace/skill/references/workspace.md","toolAction":"Viewing workspace reference","toolSummary":"Read workspace reference"}}]}
{"step_index":94,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:39:23Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-09T14:39:23Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-09T14:39:23Z\nFile Path: `file:///workspace/skill/references/workspace.md`\nTotal Lines: 22\nTotal Bytes: 2147\nShowing lines 1 to 22\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Durable workspace\n2: \n3: Keep the owner's current brief, a short current handoff, and searchable original action/evidence records in readable local files. Choose a layout appropriate to the project; the following is a starting point, not a required schema:\n4: \n5: Copy and adapt [responsibility](../assets/responsibility.md), [current handoff](../assets/current.md), [action](../assets/action.md), and [evidence](../assets/evidence.md) templates when creating a workspace. Resolve the brief in conversation before activating it; empty template fields do not supply authority or defaults.\n6: \n7: ```text\n8: brief.md\n9: current.md\n10: actions/<stable-id>.md\n11: evidence/<source-id>.<format>\n12: index.md                    # optional, generated navigation\n13: ```\n14: \n15: The handoff identifies the current objective/status, unresolved effects, active observations, relevant limits, confirmed continuation, and links needed for the next decision. Keep old detail in the underlying records; avoid repeatedly copying every plan and historical narrative into the handoff.\n16: \n17: For a consequential action, retain its stable identity, subject and conditions, intended effect and rationale, actual service request/receipt, observed result or unresolved status, relevant evidence, and next observation. Distinguish proposed, implemented, deployed, observed, adopted, and rolled-back work without forcing every task through all these stages. Include source identities, periods, measurement definitions, and important missing coverage in retained evidence.\n18: \n19: Link a correction to its earlier claim and source. Preserve the original observation and action history; date the revised interpretation and applicability. Related findings retain their originating responsibility and product. A terminated source remains terminated.\n20: \n21: Write enough before an external effect that a fresh agent can reconcile it after interruption. Store atomic current-state updates where practical; retain original evidence separately so a damaged summary can be recovered. No unique finding may live solely in an index. Rebuild or bypass stale navigation using source files. Retain history through termination until owner deletion.\n22: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":95,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:39:23Z","thinking":"**Re-examining product brief details**\n\nThe product is active, owned by Sam, and focuses on increasing sustainable net subscription revenue. There's a constraint to run at most one new experiment at a time, with a focus on refund-adjusted revenue over trial starts. Limited authority within this product, with emphasis on reversible changes based on evidence.\n\n\n**Evaluating experiment candidates**\n\nQuiet Return was considered promising before summer cleanup, while Harbor showed negative signals. Design has refreshed both proposals. The current focus is deciding which experiment to select, referencing available data and documentation. The latest QA record supports the Harbor H2 proposal, finding a critical bug in H1 resolved in H2, and no customer exposure exists for either.\n\n\n**Analyzing experiment R7 results**\n\nThe 'summer-offers' experiment (R7) initially showed positive trial start increases. However, after incorporating refund data, the mature revenue analysis revealed a 6.2% decrease below control. R7's complete record indicates no grounds for repeating the intervention in this cohort, despite early optimistic signs. The project brief emphasizes refund-adjusted revenue as the primary metric.\n\n\n**Rejecting Quiet Return retest**\n\nThe refreshed Quiet Return proposal only alters illustration colors, leaving the core discount mechanics unchanged. R7's poor performance (-6.2% refund-adjusted revenue) suggests that repeating the experiment would likely result in similar revenue losses. Existing evidence explicitly warns against applying the \"Quiet Return\" results to the current scope.\n\n**Considering Harbor for new mobile users**\n\nThe next step involves evaluating the Harbor proposal for new mobile accounts, based on prior actions and context records.\n\n\n**Analyzing Harbor experiment data**\n\nThe Harbor experiment (deployed August 10 / 2026-08-10, rolled back August 18, 2026) initially showed a -9% revenue per new account, later corrected. A significant telemetry flaw inflated the denominator. It was found that resumed sessions were counted as new, along with a UX bug that reset annual plans in permission dialogs.\n\nThe corrected analysis, after deduplication, yields a +1.8% revenue per new account, which is inconclusive given a wide confidence interval and a UX bug that still persists. This suggests that the initial negative findings were likely due to data and UX issues.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Harbor H2 experiment**\n\nDesktop account data shows a -3% revenue correction after billing retries, which is a different action and population than the mobile focus. QA confirms Harbor H2 resolves a key UX bug present in H1. Harbor H2's revenue hypothesis remains unvalidated due to previous issues.\n\nHarbor H2 should be the next experiment. The revenue hypothesis remains untested cleanly without the reset bug.\n\n\n**Confirming Harbor H2 Experiment Priority**\n\nHarbor H2's QA verification across multiple devices confirms the resolution of the critical annual plan reset bug. The central revenue hypothesis, presenting the annual card to new mobile users to increase sustainable net subscription revenue, remains unvalidated due to the presence of a UX bug in H1.\n\n**Reiterating Quiet Return Rejection**\n\nThe prior R7 trial with returning mobile subscribers, despite initial trial start gains, ultimately showed a 6.2% decrease in refund-adjusted net revenue. R7 results explicitly prioritize refund-adjusted revenue over trial starts. A minor refresh for Quiet Return offers no substantial changes to price or eligibility, which were the key factors in the R7 failure. Desktop monthly subscriber data showing \"positive\" results should not influence decisions for returning iOS mobile subscribers.\n\n\n**Preparing Harbor H2 experiment plan**\n\nNext, a controlled experiment for Harbor H2 on new US mobile accounts will be prepared. This experiment requires ensuring resumed sessions aren't double-counted as new accounts and verifying annual plan selection persistence across OS permission dialogs. Tracking refund-adjusted net revenue with a mature cohort window, and achieving sufficient statistical significance, are also essential.\n\nKey uncertainty remains the impact of H2 on net revenue, specifically the trade-off between increased annual plan selection and potential higher refund/cancellation rates. The existing data suggests a possible positive effect, but the confidence interval is too wide to determine if a net positive effect can be achieved.\n\n\n**Addressing experiment data caveats**\n\nAndroid/iOS OS fragmentation could introduce edge cases not captured in QA, potentially resetting states. Early conversion signals can be misleading; mature ledgers and refund windows need to be assessed. Ensure distinct cohort segmentation for Harbor H2, preventing overlap with other experiments using the same aliases.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"/workspace/work/decision.md","toolAction":"Checking if decision.md exists","toolSummary":"Check decision.md"}}]}
{"step_index":97,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:39:37Z","thinking":"**Checking for Necessary Files**\n\nThe target file `/workspace/work/decision.md` is not present, indicating a potential gap in required resources. Reviewing available guidelines and prior actions is required to determine the next steps and ensure that the necessary information is accounted for and that all steps are followed.\n\n\n**Analyzing Offer History and Context**\n\nReviewing the summer offers, specifically Quiet Offer (QR7), which was a 20% annual renewal discount for returning US iOS subscribers, experienced a rollback due to refund escalations after deployment.  Additionally, there's Harbor H1, an annual plan picker for new US mobile accounts, also rolled back shortly after deployment.  Both designs are present in a proposal, suggesting a possible design refresh.\n\n\n**Evaluating Harbor H2 and Quiet Return**\n\nHarbor H2, which persists annual selection, shows promise as Quality Assurance testing indicates H1's reset issue is resolved; it's a newer design that has not reached customers. Quiet Return (R7), a summer offer, initially appeared positive with trial starts at +11%, but matured data shows a -6.2% net revenue, due to refunds. The discrepancy makes a repeat implementation unlikely.\n\n\n**Evaluating Harbor's Actual Performance**\n\nInitial data showed Harbor H1 as negative, but this was flawed due to double-counting resumed sessions and a discovered bug resetting annual plan selections after OS permissions. Subsequent analysis, correcting these issues, shows a +1.8% revenue per new account, which is inconclusive. The annual plan reset bug was confirmed and directly addressed in Harbor H2. Therefore, Harbor H1's performance was negatively impacted by a significant UX bug and not inherently unsuccessful. Harbor H2 should be considered since it addresses the discovered bug. Quiet Return is eliminated from further consideration due to negative mature revenue.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Harbor H2 Experimentation**\n\nHarbor H2's annual plan selection persistence addresses the critical bug observed in H1, making it the most promising candidate for the next experiment. The core revenue hypothesis for Harbor H2 has not been tested cleanly, making further investigation essential. Preparing the experiment includes specifying instrumentation to handle session deduplication, OS permission dialog state, and refund-adjusted revenue measurement with predefined statistical power.\n\n**Evaluating Revenue and Uncertainty**\n\nThe net revenue impact of H2 remains uncertain.  The previous positive results from H1 are tainted by a bug.  The experiment should focus on resolving the observed bug, to sustainably impact net subscription revenue.\n\n\n**Examining Experiment Risks and Data**\n\nConsideration of delayed refunds and chargebacks with annual plans, previously observed, raises concerns about net revenue lift. Real-world device diversity presents potential state loss risks in edge cases, even after QA testing.\n\nCohort misattribution remains a critical risk due to overlapping names and aliases between offers, requiring careful segmentation. File paths will be cited for all sources.\n\nAnnual plan revenue may not be sustainable.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Dated recommendation and evidence analysis for the revenue responsibility evaluating Quiet Return versus Harbor H2.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# Revenue Responsibility: Offer Experiment Decision\n\n**Date:** 2026-09-08  \n**Author:** Revenue Responsibility Autonomous Agent  \n**Owner:** Sam, Product Lead  \n**Scope Reference:** [/workspace/product/brief.md](file:///workspace/product/brief.md)  \n**Status Reference:** [/workspace/product/current.md](file:///workspace/product/current.md)  \n\n---\n\n## 1. Recommendation Summary\n\nBetween the two proposals under review—**Quiet Return** (for returning mobile subscribers) and **Harbor** (for new mobile accounts)—**Harbor (Variant H2) deserves the next experiment**. **Quiet Return does not deserve an experiment**.\n\n- **Quiet Return (Variant R7)** appeared successful initially (+11% trial starts in [`record-da3a9e962e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-da3a9e962e.md)), but mature ledger analysis proved it was net-revenue destructive (**-6.2% refund-adjusted net revenue** in [`record-802325ed36`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-802325ed36.md)). The refreshed proposal in [`record-3c858d6a57`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md) retains the identical R7 discount pricing, eligibility rules, and checkout flow—altering only illustration colors. Because the economic drivers of customer dissatisfaction and refunds remain unchanged, running Quiet Return again risks predictable revenue loss.\n- **Harbor (Variant H1)** was prematurely branded a loss (-9% in [`record-783bf16383`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-783bf16383.md)) due to double-counting resumed sessions in the denominator and a confirmed UX defect where annual selections reset during the OS permission dialog. When telemetry was deduplicated in [`record-47eaba418e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-47eaba418e.md), revenue per new account was actually **+1.8%** (inconclusive), even while handicapped by the reset bug. Harbor H2 ([`record-3c858d6a57`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md)) directly resolves the permission-dialog reset (verified in QA [`record-0d1c74ca54`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md)), leaving the fundamental revenue hypothesis viable and ready for an unbiased test.\n\nPer [`brief.md`](file:///workspace/product/brief.md), standing policy permits at most one new experiment at a time, prioritizing refund-adjusted net revenue over trial starts. Harbor H2 is the sole candidate with a sound, untested revenue hypothesis and targeted defect remediation.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Relevant Prior Actions & Reconstructed Chronology\n\n### A. Quiet Return for Returning Mobile Subscribers\n\n1. **Origin & Baseline Action ([`record-b7ab79e22e`](file:///workspace/product/history/retired/summer-offers/actions/record-b7ab79e22e.md)):**\n   - **Origin:** Originating in the `summer-offers` campaign ([`/workspace/product/history/retired/summer-offers/brief.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/retired/summer-offers/brief.md), terminated 2026-07-30; historical records retained under standing revenue authority).\n   - **Aliases:** `QR7`, `returning mobile offer`, `Quiet Offer`.\n   - **Target Cohort:** US returning iOS annual subscribers.\n   - **Intervention (Variant R7):** Offered a 20% annual renewal discount upon return.\n   - **Deployment & Exposure:** Deployed on 2026-07-12 via rollout receipt `record-e4142b048e` at 50% traffic exposure. The observation period spanned July 13–19, 2026.\n   - **Rollback:** Rolled back on 2026-07-21 (receipt `record-e0da7df86e`) due to mounting customer support escalations regarding refunds.\n\n2. **Early Observation ([`record-da3a9e962e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-da3a9e962e.md)):**\n   - **Recorded:** 2026-07-20.\n   - **Initial Finding:** Trial starts increased by **+11%**, leading an analyst to headline the trial as \"promising.\" However, the record noted explicitly that retained net revenue was not yet mature.\n\n3. **Mature Ledger Correction ([`record-802325ed36`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-802325ed36.md)):**\n   - **Recorded:** 2026-08-04.\n   - **Corrected Finding:** Followed the July 13–19 exposure cohort with matched refund ledger data through August 2, 2026. While the +11% trial-start volume was real, **refund-adjusted net revenue was 6.2% below control (-6.2%)**. \n   - **Applicability & Conclusion:** The matched ledger was confirmed complete for this cohort. The record stated definitively: *\"No price or eligibility changes justify repeating R7 in this cohort.\"*\n\n4. **Irrelevant Name Reuse Warning ([`record-3965c8ff16`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-3965c8ff16.md)):**\n   - **Recorded:** 2026-09-06.\n   - **Context:** A recent correction noted a +4% net revenue lift under the name \"Quiet Return\" for action `record-cf96fad305`.\n   - **Separation:** This report tested variant W3 on **US returning desktop monthly subscribers** exposed August 20–27, 2026. The record explicitly cautions: *\"This report does not cover record-b7ab79e22e, R7, returning iOS annual subscribers, or July exposures.\"*\n\n5. **September Design Proposal ([`record-3c858d6a57`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md)):**\n   - **Dated:** 2026-09-02.\n   - **Change Proposed:** Maintains identical R7 pricing (20% discount), identical eligibility, and identical mobile checkout flow; only illustration colors were updated.\n\n---\n\n### B. Harbor for New Mobile Accounts\n\n1. **Baseline Action ([`record-dc92607ff3`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-dc92607ff3.md)):**\n   - **Aliases:** `Anchor plan picker`, `annual card`, `Harbor H1`.\n   - **Target Cohort:** New US mobile accounts.\n   - **Intervention (Harbor H1):** Presented an annual subscription selection card / anchor plan picker during initial mobile onboarding.\n   - **Deployment & Rollout:** Deployed August 10 [year not stated in record; preserved as August 10], rollout record `record-eb44fddf46`.\n   - **Rollback:** Rolled back August 18 [year not stated in record; preserved as August 18], receipt `record-4cd3618639`.\n\n2. **Initial Inaccurate Evidence ([`record-783bf16383`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-783bf16383.md)):**\n   - **Recorded:** August 18 [year not stated in record; preserved as August 18].\n   - **Observation Window:** August 11–17 [year not stated in record; preserved as August 11–17].\n   - **Initial Metric:** Revenue per new account reported at **-9%** (with no confidence claim).\n   - **Telemetry & UX Failures Identified:**\n     1. Resumed app sessions were double-counted as new accounts in telemetry, artificially inflating the denominator.\n     2. In session recordings, 7 of 12 reviewed user sessions that encountered the OS permission dialog had their chosen annual plan selection reset to default.\n   - This flawed initial report was the source of [`current.md`](file:///workspace/product/current.md)'s note that \"Harbor looked negative.\"\n\n3. **Telemetry Deduplication & Correction ([`record-47eaba418e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-47eaba418e.md)):**\n   - **Recorded:** 2026-08-24.\n   - **Correction:** Corrected `record-783bf16383` for `record-dc92607ff3` H1 on the identical August 11–17 cohort.\n   - **Corrected Metric:** Deduplicated revenue per new account was **+1.8%** with a wide interval spanning harm and benefit (inconclusive).\n   - **Finding:** Rollback receipt `record-4cd3618639` remained an actual historical event, and the permission reset bug in recordings was confirmed genuine. The record cautioned: *\"Do not label Harbor a demonstrated loss or win.\"*\n\n4. **Irrelevant Name Overlap Warning ([`record-0f6fbbab4e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-0f6fbbab4e.md)):**\n   - **Dated:** 2026-09-07.\n   - **Context:** Action `record-d3b97d8b03` labeled \"Harbor\" on **returning desktop accounts** (exposed August 25–31, 2026) showed -3% corrected revenue after billing retry inflation.\n   - **Separation:** The record explicitly states: *\"The product name overlaps record-dc92607ff3, but this is a different action and population.\"*\n\n5. **September Design & Defect Fix Proposal ([`record-3c858d6a57`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md)):**\n   - **Dated:** 2026-09-02.\n   - **Change Proposed (Harbor H2):** Persist the user's annual plan selection before the OS permission dialog and restore it upon resume.\n   - **QA Verification:** QA record `record-0d1c74ca54` reproduced H1's reset bug and verified it was completely eliminated in H2 across 18 supported-device runs.\n   - **Current State:** H2 has not yet been exposed to customers; the underlying revenue hypothesis remains untested.\n\n---\n\n## 3. What the Evidence Supports Now\n\n| Evaluation Dimension | Quiet Return (R7 refreshed) | Harbor (H2 refreshed) | Evidence Sources |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Historical Net Revenue** | **-6.2% refund-adjusted revenue** below control (matured ledger complete). | **+1.8% deduplicated revenue per account** (inconclusive; wide confidence interval). | [`record-802325ed36`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-802325ed36.md), [`record-47eaba418e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-47eaba418e.md) |\n| **Top-of-Funnel Metric** | +11% trial starts (transient, misleading). | Flawed initial -9% report caused by double-counted resumed sessions in denominator. | [`record-da3a9e962e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-da3a9e962e.md), [`record-783bf16383`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-783bf16383.md) |\n| **Root Cause of Past Defect** | Structural: 20% renewal discount caused refund requests and post-trial cancellations. | Technical/UX: App reset user plan choice back to default upon OS permission dialog (7/12 sessions). | [`record-b7ab79e22e`](file:///workspace/product/history/retired/summer-offers/actions/record-b7ab79e22e.md), [`record-783bf16383`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-783bf16383.md) |\n| **Substance of Refresh** | Superficial: same price, eligibility, and checkout flow; changed only illustration colors. | Functional: persists plan selection across OS permission dialogs; validated in QA (`record-0d1c74ca54`). | [`record-3c858d6a57`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md) |\n| **Hypothesis Viability** | **Invalidated:** Mature evidence demonstrates economic harm under R7 terms. | **Untested & Promising:** Core hypothesis of annual plan presentation has never been run without the UX defect. | [`record-802325ed36`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-802325ed36.md), [`record-3c858d6a57`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md) |\n\n### Key Analytical Conclusions:\n1. **Quiet Return R7 must not be repeated:** The standing scope mandate in [`brief.md`](file:///workspace/product/brief.md) explicitly establishes that *\"Refund-adjusted revenue matters more than trial starts.\"* R7 generated a high volume of signups that subsequently refunded or escalated, reducing net revenue by 6.2%. Because the September proposal makes no changes to pricing, discounting, or eligibility, cosmetic illustration changes cannot overcome this structural deficit.\n2. **Harbor's negative reputation in `current.md` was based on obsolete data:** As of the 2026-08-19 handoff, Harbor appeared negative because only `record-783bf16383` was known. The subsequent 2026-08-24 correction ([`record-47eaba418e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-47eaba418e.md)) proved Harbor was not a loser, while the design documentation ([`record-3c858d6a57`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md)) confirmed the existence and resolution of the critical permission-dialog bug.\n3. **Desktop cohort outcomes do not translate to mobile cohorts:** Neither the +4% desktop result for Quiet Return W3 ([`record-3965c8ff16`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-3965c8ff16.md)) nor the -3% desktop result for Harbor (`record-0f6fbbab4e`) should influence the decision for mobile cohorts.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Next Useful Action\n\nIn accordance with standing authority under [`brief.md`](file:///workspace/product/brief.md) (investigate evidence, choose ordinary objectives, and prepare reversible changes within this product, with no live external actions or production mutations authorized in this review snapshot):\n\n1. **Select Objective:** Authorize the preparation of an experiment for **Harbor H2** targeting **new US mobile accounts**.\n2. **Instrumentation Specifications Required for H2:**\n   - **Telemetry Deduplication Guard:** Implement a persistent account/device token in the experiment analytics harness to prevent resumed application sessions from being logged as new accounts in the denominator (remedying the flaw in [`record-783bf16383`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-783bf16383.md)).\n   - **Permission Flow State Telemetry:** Emit explicit telemetry events logging plan selection prior to permission dialog display and verify plan restoration upon app resume to monitor whether the QA fix ([`record-0d1c74ca54`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md)) holds under live operating conditions.\n   - **Cohort Isolation:** Ensure routing filters strictly target new US mobile accounts, isolating the variant from desktop cohorts or returning subscriber tests.\n3. **Required Evidence for Decision:**\n   - **Mature Refund-Adjusted Revenue Window:** Run the experiment for a minimum duration that covers the initial billing cycle plus refund maturation (minimum 14–21 days post-exposure), avoiding premature declarations based on trial starts.\n   - **Confidence Intervals on Net Revenue:** Pre-specify a sample size capable of distinguishing whether deduplicated revenue per new account exceeds control with statistical precision, resolving the inconclusive wide interval from H1.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Important Uncertainty\n\n1. **Net Revenue Effect of Removing the Reset Friction:** While Harbor H1 achieved +1.8% deduplicated revenue despite the bug, its confidence interval spanned both negative and positive territory. While H2 ensures users who select annual plans actually check out with annual plans, whether new mobile accounts retain these subscriptions or request refunds upon billing is untested.\n2. **Live Device / OS Fragmentation:** QA tested H2 across 18 supported devices ([`record-0d1c74ca54`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md)). However, edge-case Android memory reclamation or unusual iOS permission dialog lifecycle interruptions under low-memory conditions could still cause unhandled state drops in the wild.\n3. **Refund Lag & Ledger Maturation:** Early funnel gains can hide late refunds (as happened with Quiet Return in [`record-802325ed36`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-802325ed36.md)). Any rollout must retain a rollback safeguard if early chargebacks or refund escalations exceed control thresholds.\n4. **Historical Unknown Dates:** In accordance with evidence preservation standards, source records [`record-dc92607ff3`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-dc92607ff3.md) and [`record-783bf16383`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-783bf16383.md) lack year stamps on certain deployment, exposure, and recording dates (e.g., \"August 10\", \"August 18\", \"August 11–17\"). They have been preserved as recorded without inventing missing timestamps.\n","Description":"Write dated decision recommendation to /workspace/work/decision.md analyzing Quiet Return vs Harbor H2 based on retained history and evidence.","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"/workspace/work/decision.md","toolAction":"Writing decision.md","toolSummary":"Create decision recommendation file"}}]}
{"step_index":99,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:40:01Z","thinking":"**Correcting artifact path usage**\n\nThe error indicates `ArtifactMetadata` should only be used for artifacts within the designated directory. Realized that the file being created is a normal project file and should not include `ArtifactMetadata`. This means there's a problem with the file writing command; it needs to be updated to exclude the metadata in this specific case.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"cat << 'EOF' > /workspace/work/decision.md\n# Revenue Responsibility: Offer Experiment Decision\n\n**Date:** 2026-09-08  \n**Author:** Revenue Responsibility Autonomous Agent  \n**Owner:** Sam, Product Lead  \n**Scope Reference:** [/workspace/product/brief.md](file:///workspace/product/brief.md)  \n**Status Reference:** [/workspace/product/current.md](file:///workspace/product/current.md)  \n\n---\n\n## 1. Recommendation Summary\n\nBetween the two proposals under review—**Quiet Return** (for returning mobile subscribers) and **Harbor** (for new mobile accounts)—**Harbor (Variant H2) deserves the next experiment**. **Quiet Return does not deserve an experiment**.\n\n- **Quiet Return (Variant R7)** appeared successful initially (+11% trial starts in [`record-da3a9e962e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-da3a9e962e.md)), but mature ledger analysis proved it was net-revenue destructive (**-6.2% refund-adjusted net revenue** in [`record-802325ed36`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-802325ed36.md)). The refreshed proposal in [`record-3c858d6a57`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md) retains the identical R7 discount pricing, eligibility rules, and checkout flow—altering only illustration colors. Because the economic drivers of customer dissatisfaction and refunds remain unchanged, running Quiet Return again risks predictable revenue loss.\n- **Harbor (Variant H1)** was prematurely branded a loss (-9% in [`record-783bf16383`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-783bf16383.md)) due to double-counting resumed sessions in the denominator and a confirmed UX defect where annual selections reset during the OS permission dialog. When telemetry was deduplicated in [`record-47eaba418e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-47eaba418e.md), revenue per new account was actually **+1.8%** (inconclusive), even while handicapped by the reset bug. Harbor H2 ([`record-3c858d6a57`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md)) directly resolves the permission-dialog reset (verified in QA [`record-0d1c74ca54`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md)), leaving the fundamental revenue hypothesis viable and ready for an unbiased test.\n\nPer [`brief.md`](file:///workspace/product/brief.md), standing policy permits at most one new experiment at a time, prioritizing refund-adjusted net revenue over trial starts. Harbor H2 is the sole candidate with a sound, untested revenue hypothesis and targeted defect remediation.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Relevant Prior Actions & Reconstructed Chronology\n\n### A. Quiet Return for Returning Mobile Subscribers\n\n1. **Origin & Baseline Action ([`record-b7ab79e22e`](file:///workspace/product/history/retired/summer-offers/actions/record-b7ab79e22e.md)):**\n   - **Origin:** Originating in the `summer-offers` campaign ([`/workspace/product/history/retired/summer-offers/brief.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/retired/summer-offers/brief.md), terminated 2026-07-30; historical records retained under standing revenue authority).\n   - **Aliases:** `QR7`, `returning mobile offer`, `Quiet Offer`.\n   - **Target Cohort:** US returning iOS annual subscribers.\n   - **Intervention (Variant R7):** Offered a 20% annual renewal discount upon return.\n   - **Deployment & Exposure:** Deployed on 2026-07-12 via rollout receipt `record-e4142b048e` at 50% traffic exposure. The observation period spanned July 13–19, 2026.\n   - **Rollback:** Rolled back on 2026-07-21 (receipt `record-e0da7df86e`) due to mounting customer support escalations regarding refunds.\n\n2. **Early Observation ([`record-da3a9e962e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-da3a9e962e.md)):**\n   - **Recorded:** 2026-07-20.\n   - **Initial Finding:** Trial starts increased by **+11%**, leading an analyst to headline the trial as \"promising.\" However, the record noted explicitly that retained net revenue was not yet mature.\n\n3. **Mature Ledger Correction ([`record-802325ed36`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-802325ed36.md)):**\n   - **Recorded:** 2026-08-04.\n   - **Corrected Finding:** Followed the July 13–19 exposure cohort with matched refund ledger data through August 2, 2026. While the +11% trial-start volume was real, **refund-adjusted net revenue was 6.2% below control (-6.2%)**. \n   - **Applicability & Conclusion:** The matched ledger was confirmed complete for this cohort. The record stated definitively: *\"No price or eligibility changes justify repeating R7 in this cohort.\"*\n\n4. **Irrelevant Name Reuse Warning ([`record-3965c8ff16`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-3965c8ff16.md)):**\n   - **Recorded:** 2026-09-06.\n   - **Context:** A recent correction noted a +4% net revenue lift under the name \"Quiet Return\" for action `record-cf96fad305`.\n   - **Separation:** This report tested variant W3 on **US returning desktop monthly subscribers** exposed August 20–27, 2026. The record explicitly cautions: *\"This report does not cover record-b7ab79e22e, R7, returning iOS annual subscribers, or July exposures.\"*\n\n5. **September Design Proposal ([`record-3c858d6a57`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md)):**\n   - **Dated:** 2026-09-02.\n   - **Change Proposed:** Maintains identical R7 pricing (20% discount), identical eligibility, and identical mobile checkout flow; only illustration colors were updated.\n\n---\n\n### B. Harbor for New Mobile Accounts\n\n1. **Baseline Action ([`record-dc92607ff3`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-dc92607ff3.md)):**\n   - **Aliases:** `Anchor plan picker`, `annual card`, `Harbor H1`.\n   - **Target Cohort:** New US mobile accounts.\n   - **Intervention (Harbor H1):** Presented an annual subscription selection card / anchor plan picker during initial mobile onboarding.\n   - **Deployment & Rollout:** Deployed August 10 [year not stated in record; preserved as August 10], rollout record `record-eb44fddf46`.\n   - **Rollback:** Rolled back August 18 [year not stated in record; preserved as August 18], receipt `record-4cd3618639`.\n\n2. **Initial Inaccurate Evidence ([`record-783bf16383`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-783bf16383.md)):**\n   - **Recorded:** August 18 [year not stated in record; preserved as August 18].\n   - **Observation Window:** August 11–17 [year not stated in record; preserved as August 11–17].\n   - **Initial Metric:** Revenue per new account reported at **-9%** (with no confidence claim).\n   - **Telemetry & UX Failures Identified:**\n     1. Resumed app sessions were double-counted as new accounts in telemetry, artificially inflating the denominator.\n     2. In session recordings, 7 of 12 reviewed user sessions that encountered the OS permission dialog had their chosen annual plan selection reset to default.\n   - This flawed initial report was the source of [`current.md`](file:///workspace/product/current.md)'s note that \"Harbor looked negative.\"\n\n3. **Telemetry Deduplication & Correction ([`record-47eaba418e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-47eaba418e.md)):**\n   - **Recorded:** 2026-08-24.\n   - **Correction:** Corrected `record-783bf16383` for `record-dc92607ff3` H1 on the identical August 11–17 cohort.\n   - **Corrected Metric:** Deduplicated revenue per new account was **+1.8%** with a wide interval spanning harm and benefit (inconclusive).\n   - **Finding:** Rollback receipt `record-4cd3618639` remained an actual historical event, and the permission reset bug in recordings was confirmed genuine. The record cautioned: *\"Do not label Harbor a demonstrated loss or win.\"*\n\n4. **Irrelevant Name Overlap Warning ([`record-0f6fbbab4e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-0f6fbbab4e.md)):**\n   - **Dated:** 2026-09-07.\n   - **Context:** Action `record-d3b97d8b03` labeled \"Harbor\" on **returning desktop accounts** (exposed August 25–31, 2026) showed -3% corrected revenue after billing retry inflation.\n   - **Separation:** The record explicitly states: *\"The product name overlaps record-dc92607ff3, but this is a different action and population.\"*\n\n5. **September Design & Defect Fix Proposal ([`record-3c858d6a57`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md)):**\n   - **Dated:** 2026-09-02.\n   - **Change Proposed (Harbor H2):** Persist the user's annual plan selection before the OS permission dialog and restore it upon resume.\n   - **QA Verification:** QA record `record-0d1c74ca54` reproduced H1's reset bug and verified it was completely eliminated in H2 across 18 supported-device runs.\n   - **Current State:** H2 has not yet been exposed to customers; the underlying revenue hypothesis remains untested.\n\n---\n\n## 3. What the Evidence Supports Now\n\n| Evaluation Dimension | Quiet Return (R7 refreshed) | Harbor (H2 refreshed) | Evidence Sources |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Historical Net Revenue** | **-6.2% refund-adjusted revenue** below control (matured ledger complete). | **+1.8% deduplicated revenue per account** (inconclusive; wide confidence interval). | [`record-802325ed36`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-802325ed36.md), [`record-47eaba418e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-47eaba418e.md) |\n| **Top-of-Funnel Metric** | +11% trial starts (transient, misleading). | Flawed initial -9% report caused by double-counted resumed sessions in denominator. | [`record-da3a9e962e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-da3a9e962e.md), [`record-783bf16383`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-783bf16383.md) |\n| **Root Cause of Past Defect** | Structural: 20% renewal discount caused refund requests and post-trial cancellations. | Technical/UX: App reset user plan choice back to default upon OS permission dialog (7/12 sessions). | [`record-b7ab79e22e`](file:///workspace/product/history/retired/summer-offers/actions/record-b7ab79e22e.md), [`record-783bf16383`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-783bf16383.md) |\n| **Substance of Refresh** | Superficial: same price, eligibility, and checkout flow; changed only illustration colors. | Functional: persists plan selection across OS permission dialogs; validated in QA (`record-0d1c74ca54`). | [`record-3c858d6a57`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md) |\n| **Hypothesis Viability** | **Invalidated:** Mature evidence demonstrates economic harm under R7 terms. | **Untested & Promising:** Core hypothesis of annual plan presentation has never been run without the UX defect. | [`record-802325ed36`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-802325ed36.md), [`record-3c858d6a57`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md) |\n\n### Key Analytical Conclusions:\n1. **Quiet Return R7 must not be repeated:** The standing scope mandate in [`brief.md`](file:///workspace/product/brief.md) explicitly establishes that *\"Refund-adjusted revenue matters more than trial starts.\"* R7 generated a high volume of signups that subsequently refunded or escalated, reducing net revenue by 6.2%. Because the September proposal makes no changes to pricing, discounting, or eligibility, cosmetic illustration changes cannot overcome this structural deficit.\n2. **Harbor's negative reputation in `current.md` was based on obsolete data:** As of the 2026-08-19